<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n23879" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in-sŏcĭābĭlis</span></b> ,
			e, adj., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>that cannot be joined together</i>, <i>unsociable</i>, <i>incompatible</i>
			(mostly post-Aug.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">gens,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					37, 1</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">diversae, insociabilesque naturae arborum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					17, 19, 30, § 137</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">anum insociabilem nurui efficiebat,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tac. A.
					4, 12 <i>fin.</i></span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">regnum (with discordiae),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 13, 17</span></i>
			; 15, 68.</div>
